## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | test/cli/agent_cli_waiting_integration_test.dart | 🚨 blocking the two new real process integration tests fail on the exact host class this pr targets ps capable linux — boot re adoption never fires so the ac1 ac2 flows under test cannot engage reproduced twice on linux with working ps setsid this sandbox — same host class as ci linux ❌ bash job stop on an adopted setsid job kills the whole group and clears the manifest issue 2260 ac1 bad state no element — agent cli waiting integration test dart 194 12 single ❌ stop of a non group leader adopted job keeps the manifest record issue 2260 ac2 bad state no element — agent cli waiting integration test dart 271 12 single → 91 tests passed 2 failed identical in both runs root cause in unchanged code first exposed by these new tests pidstartsnapshot lib src env process probe io dart 29 35 returns the raw ps o lstart line including its trailing newline every table parser it is compared against trims probeliveprocesses at agent cli waiting dart 683 698 processdetailtablesnapshot s lstart columns verified directly single tue nov 17 21 43 02 2026 n table tue nov 17 21 43 02 2026 equal false so entryalive agent cli waiting dart 358 372 compares recorded …2026 n actual …2026 → false → the live entry is judged recycled and dropped at boot stale job entry dropped instead of being re adopted consequences in order of impact 1 this pr s own scenario is non functional in production ac1 requires a previous run s setsid job to be re adopted at boot before the stop can kill its group on every host where the probe works the manifest entry is dropped first — the group kill path is never reached only the boot sweep s live leader skip saves the running job from a wrongful reap 2 issue 2201 ac5 re adoption is dead on probe capable hosts — the same mismatch means every manifest entry recorded via pidstart agent cli waiting dart 705 stores the newline form is discarded at the next boot even while its process runs 3 even if reconcile kept the entry the boot adopted starttag would carry the newline into adoptedshelljob and misfire the 478 recycled guard in refresh stop against probelivenesstable s trimmed lstart — first poll would mark a live job gone the tests never ran green anywhere on the author s mac they skip psavailable false and on ci linux they fail as above — the pr as is ships red ci fix one line root cause trim in the producer — pidstartsnapshot returns out trim — aligning the single pid probe with both table parsers every comparison site entryalive refresh stop adoptrunningentry then agrees with no further changes and both new tests pass please also consider a regression unit test pinning pidstartsnapshot s trimmed form so the parsers can t drift apart again |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/tools/builtin_tools_bash.dart | 💡 suggestion stopped the leader can be false when the leader itself is still in the survivor list stopdetachedprocess scans the group after the term→400 ms→kill rounds and reports every row with pgid pid that is not a zombie if the kill round has not taken effect yet a member in uninterruptible sleep — d state on nfs fuse is the classic case — ignores both signals until it leaves the kernel wait the leader s own row survives the filter and comes back in the list the tool result then prints stopped the leader id — 1 process group member s still running pid leader pid … the next boot reaps the survivors two claims are wrong in that corner the leader did not stop and the next boot will not reap anything either — reaporphanjobgroups skips live leaders this is exactly the honesty class ac2 was written for the survivor pids themselves are surfaced correctly so the model still gets actionable data — hence suggestion not blocker cheap refinement when the scan s survivors include pid itself emit a distinct text stop signaled the group leader pid n is still alive — kill not yet effective and let the settle notice stay in the unverified mode evidence that would raise this one level if d state stops are a realistic workload for your hosts treat it as ⚠️ — the entry is also marked gone settled while the leader lives |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

